1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,296
Why did you do that?

2
00:00:02,496 --> 00:00:03,540
No reason.

3
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:05,673
Why are you in a bad mood?

4
00:00:05,874 --> 00:00:06,917
No reason.

5
00:00:07,468 --> 00:00:09,556
Why didn't you answer their call?

6
00:00:09,756 --> 00:00:11,088
I just didn't.

7
00:00:11,638 --> 00:00:15,274
When you open the fridge, take nothing out, and close it again.

8
00:00:15,474 --> 00:00:20,478
When you unlock your phone, forget what you were going to do, and just keep scrolling.

9
00:00:20,678 --> 00:00:24,026
An evening when your heart sinks for no reason at all.

10
00:00:24,226 --> 00:00:27,862
We cover every one of these moments with the same words.

11
00:00:28,061 --> 00:00:29,141
Just because.

12
00:00:29,691 --> 00:00:32,895
But the truth is, there is no just because.

13
00:00:33,096 --> 00:00:39,288
Today, I'll talk about how simply noticing these two small words can begin to change your life.

14
00:00:39,837 --> 00:00:49,845
And I'll tell you the story of someone whose heart always grew heavy around one particular smell, and how they found the real reason behind their just because.

15
00:00:50,995 --> 00:00:54,919
We are souls who came to this Earth to experience.

16
00:00:55,120 --> 00:01:01,708
And here on Earth, every thought, every word, every action, and every feeling of the soul has a reason.

17
00:01:02,257 --> 00:01:04,813
Why you like something, and why you don't.

18
00:01:05,013 --> 00:01:07,893
What you want to do, and what you want to choose.

19
00:01:08,094 --> 00:01:11,118
What you want, and what you don't want.

20
00:01:11,318 --> 00:01:18,086
Just as even a single leaf floating on a pond has long roots reaching down beneath the water.

21
00:01:18,636 --> 00:01:20,832
It's just that you can't see those roots.

22
00:01:21,032 --> 00:01:23,588
So we say, just because.

23
00:01:24,137 --> 00:01:28,241
So when we say just because, what we really mean is this.

24
00:01:28,442 --> 00:01:29,917
I don't know the reason yet.

25
00:01:31,067 --> 00:01:33,047
Imagine someone like this.

26
00:01:33,597 --> 00:01:39,573
Whenever they walked past a hospital, or caught the smell of disinfectant somewhere, their heart just sank.

27
00:01:39,773 --> 00:01:41,213
They didn't know why.

28
00:01:41,413 --> 00:01:45,373
It's probably just my mood, they'd tell themselves, and move on.

29
00:01:45,923 --> 00:01:49,919
Then one day, this time, they decided not to let it go.

30
00:01:50,470 --> 00:01:55,510
They sat in a quiet room, closed their eyes, and took a few deep breaths.

31
00:01:55,710 --> 00:01:57,905
And they gently asked the one inside.

32
00:01:58,455 --> 00:01:59,139
Hey.

33
00:01:59,339 --> 00:02:02,363
Why does your heart grow so heavy whenever you smell this?

34
00:02:02,913 --> 00:02:05,073
At first, there was no answer.

35
00:02:05,273 --> 00:02:06,929
But they didn't rush.

36
00:02:07,129 --> 00:02:08,389
They simply waited.

37
00:02:08,939 --> 00:02:12,467
Then a spot in their chest began to tighten, just a little.

38
00:02:12,667 --> 00:02:14,287
So they asked that feeling.

39
00:02:14,487 --> 00:02:16,467
How long have you been there?

40
00:02:17,017 --> 00:02:21,122
Then, a forgotten scene slowly rose up.

41
00:02:21,321 --> 00:02:25,857
White walls, a cold bed, a faint light at the end of the hallway.

42
00:02:26,057 --> 00:02:31,709
It was the hospital room where they had stayed for a long time, as a very small child.

43
00:02:32,259 --> 00:02:35,499
The night their mother went home, and they were left alone.

44
00:02:35,699 --> 00:02:40,775
That child was scared and lonely, but believed they weren't allowed to cry.

45
00:02:40,975 --> 00:02:44,359
So they swallowed that feeling, all of it.

46
00:02:44,909 --> 00:02:48,653
That smell had been bringing back the feeling they swallowed that night.

47
00:02:48,853 --> 00:02:50,761
It was never just because.

48
00:02:51,911 --> 00:02:54,863
Our own just becauses are the same.

49
00:02:55,413 --> 00:02:59,157
On the way home from work, you're irritated for no reason.

50
00:02:59,357 --> 00:03:05,153
Look closely, and you skipped a real lunch, and in a meeting, what you said was brushed aside like it was nothing.

51
00:03:05,353 --> 00:03:10,573
The truth is, you were exhausted, and you wanted someone to understand how you felt.

52
00:03:11,123 --> 00:03:14,759
You just met someone, and you don't like them, for no reason.

53
00:03:14,959 --> 00:03:19,963
Look closely, and maybe the way they talk reminds you of someone who once hurt you.

54
00:03:20,513 --> 00:03:24,618
Things are going well, and still, you feel anxious for no reason.

55
00:03:24,817 --> 00:03:32,233
Look closely, and maybe there's a very young you inside, who believed you had to do well to be loved.

56
00:03:32,784 --> 00:03:36,744
Behind every just because, there is always a story.

57
00:03:36,944 --> 00:03:42,667
Something you went through, the conclusion you drew back then, and the beliefs that conclusion created.

58
00:03:42,868 --> 00:03:50,140
That story is quietly moving your feelings, your thoughts, and your actions, right now.

59
00:03:51,290 --> 00:03:53,450
But we rarely look at that story.

60
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,952
We're usually far more sensitive to what's outside.

61
00:03:57,152 --> 00:04:01,940
Other people's faces, other people's words, the news of the world.

62
00:04:02,140 --> 00:04:05,884
All day long, our attention points outward.

63
00:04:06,434 --> 00:04:11,546
In a single day, you check other people's updates dozens of times.

64
00:04:11,746 --> 00:04:15,634
But how many times did you ask your own heart, how was today?

65
00:04:16,184 --> 00:04:19,496
We're numb to what's actually happening inside us.

66
00:04:19,696 --> 00:04:22,252
And that's where just because comes from.

67
00:04:22,802 --> 00:04:26,078
Now it's time to change the order.

68
00:04:26,278 --> 00:04:28,834
Inside first, before outside.

69
00:04:29,034 --> 00:04:30,150
And more of it.

70
00:04:30,349 --> 00:04:35,210
Becoming more sensitive, more particular, about knowing yourself.

71
00:04:35,409 --> 00:04:37,282
Where did this feeling come from?

72
00:04:37,482 --> 00:04:38,777
Why did I say that?

73
00:04:38,977 --> 00:04:40,489
Not letting it slip by.

74
00:04:41,039 --> 00:04:45,575
People on the spiritual path sometimes call this escaping the Matrix.

75
00:04:45,775 --> 00:04:53,515
The thoughts the world decided for you, the beliefs others planted in you, the reactions that repeat without you noticing.

76
00:04:53,715 --> 00:04:57,891
Living inside all that, without knowing why, just because.

77
00:04:58,091 --> 00:04:59,495
That is the Matrix.

78
00:05:00,045 --> 00:05:03,033
But the door out of the Matrix isn't outside.

79
00:05:03,233 --> 00:05:05,573
The only way out is in.

80
00:05:05,773 --> 00:05:09,769
The more you come to know yourself, the further you walk out of the Matrix.

81
00:05:10,919 --> 00:05:12,215
So how do you go in?

82
00:05:12,415 --> 00:05:15,619
Do what the person with the smell of disinfectant did.

83
00:05:16,169 --> 00:05:19,949
When the words just because come up, pause once and ask.

84
00:05:20,150 --> 00:05:21,013
Why?

85
00:05:21,563 --> 00:05:26,280
Not like you're scolding yourself, but gently, like asking a curious friend.

86
00:05:26,479 --> 00:05:29,683
And when an answer comes, ask once more.

87
00:05:29,883 --> 00:05:31,179
And why is that?

88
00:05:31,729 --> 00:05:32,701
For example.

89
00:05:32,902 --> 00:05:34,090
I just put it off.

90
00:05:34,289 --> 00:05:35,153
Why?

91
00:05:35,354 --> 00:05:36,686
I didn't want to do it.

92
00:05:36,885 --> 00:05:37,749
Why?

93
00:05:37,950 --> 00:05:40,578
Honestly, it felt overwhelming.

94
00:05:40,777 --> 00:05:42,073
And why is that?

95
00:05:42,273 --> 00:05:43,929
I was afraid I'd fail.

96
00:05:44,479 --> 00:05:50,924
Ask just three times, and the real feeling hiding behind just because shows itself.

97
00:05:51,473 --> 00:05:54,857
If the answer doesn't come right away, don't rush.

98
00:05:55,057 --> 00:05:55,813
Wait.

99
00:05:56,013 --> 00:05:59,433
Sometimes your body answers before your thoughts do.

100
00:05:59,633 --> 00:06:04,169
A tightness in your chest, a lump in your throat, your shoulders stiffening.

101
00:06:04,719 --> 00:06:07,275
That is self-awareness.

102
00:06:07,825 --> 00:06:10,849
Awareness isn't only for when you meditate.

103
00:06:11,049 --> 00:06:15,873
When you eat, when you speak, when you write someone back, when you walk.

104
00:06:16,073 --> 00:06:20,285
In every moment of the day, being just a little more awake.

105
00:06:20,835 --> 00:06:23,391
Oh, I'm thinking this right now.

106
00:06:23,592 --> 00:06:25,716
Oh, I'm about to say this.

107
00:06:25,916 --> 00:06:28,040
Oh, I'm sighing again.

108
00:06:28,590 --> 00:06:30,102
You don't have to be perfect.

109
00:06:30,301 --> 00:06:33,614
Just notice one more time today than you did yesterday.

110
00:06:33,813 --> 00:06:39,141
As those awake moments grow, just because fades, and the inside of you grows brighter.

111
00:06:39,342 --> 00:06:42,150
Awakening isn't somewhere far away.

112
00:06:42,349 --> 00:06:46,669
It's coming to know, one piece at a time, the parts of you that you didn't know.

113
00:06:47,820 --> 00:06:50,808
If you don't know the reason, you can't change it.

114
00:06:51,008 --> 00:06:52,520
It's just the way it is.

115
00:06:52,719 --> 00:06:58,732
So the same wounds, the same reactions, the same choices, keep repeating.

116
00:06:59,282 --> 00:07:02,666
But once you know the reason, things change.

117
00:07:02,866 --> 00:07:08,193
If you choose to, you can heal that wound, and you can rewrite that old story.

118
00:07:08,744 --> 00:07:17,996
The person whose heart sank at the smell of disinfectant, only after knowing the reason, could finally speak to that little child who couldn't even cry that night.

119
00:07:18,195 --> 00:07:19,635
You were so scared.

120
00:07:19,835 --> 00:07:21,311
It's okay to cry now.

121
00:07:21,511 --> 00:07:22,663
I'm here.

122
00:07:22,863 --> 00:07:26,427
And after that, the smell no longer pulled their heart down.

123
00:07:26,977 --> 00:07:29,533
There's a line often attributed to Carl Jung.

124
00:07:29,733 --> 00:07:35,277
Until you make the unconscious conscious, it will direct your life, and you will call it fate.

125
00:07:35,827 --> 00:07:41,299
The moment you notice the story that was trapped inside just because, it's no longer fate.

126
00:07:41,499 --> 00:07:43,947
It becomes a choice you can make.

127
00:07:44,497 --> 00:07:47,881
And reasons don't only hide in wounds.

128
00:07:48,081 --> 00:07:51,969
If something draws you for no reason, don't let that slip by either.

129
00:07:52,169 --> 00:07:52,997
Ask.

130
00:07:53,198 --> 00:07:54,854
Why am I drawn to this?

131
00:07:55,054 --> 00:07:59,878
In that answer, you may find what your soul wants to experience in this life.

132
00:08:00,428 --> 00:08:07,556
When you know that reason, what you truly want becomes clear, and you can choose the life you want, more clearly.

133
00:08:08,106 --> 00:08:12,750
Awareness becomes awakening, and awakening becomes creation.

134
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:16,406
That's how we create our own lives, here on Earth.

135
00:08:17,556 --> 00:08:21,480
And the more you know yourself, the more you understand yourself.

136
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:24,092
Oh, so that's why I did that.

137
00:08:24,642 --> 00:08:27,486
Once you understand, you can't hate.

138
00:08:27,686 --> 00:08:31,178
The more you understand yourself, the more you love yourself.

139
00:08:31,728 --> 00:08:39,432
When you love yourself, your heart becomes peaceful, you become happy, and your soul is filled from somewhere deep inside.

140
00:08:39,982 --> 00:08:44,086
And when you're that full, love and abundance overflow on their own.

141
00:08:44,285 --> 00:08:47,489
Not squeezed out by force, but spilling over.

142
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:49,551
And here's the beautiful part.

143
00:08:49,752 --> 00:08:54,935
Once you know the reasons behind your own just because, you start to see other people's too.

144
00:08:55,136 --> 00:08:56,900
They must have their reasons too.

145
00:08:57,449 --> 00:09:01,914
From then on, you can share with others naturally, and truly help them.

146
00:09:02,113 --> 00:09:05,389
It all begins with knowing yourself.

147
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:10,175
So starting today, try just three things.

148
00:09:10,726 --> 00:09:17,494
One, when the words just because come out of your mouth, pause, and ask inside.

149
00:09:17,694 --> 00:09:18,990
What's the real reason?

150
00:09:19,540 --> 00:09:26,127
Two, before bed, write down one just because from today, and ask why, three times.

151
00:09:26,678 --> 00:09:30,818
Three, if you find the reason, say this to it.

152
00:09:31,018 --> 00:09:32,494
Thank you for showing me.

153
00:09:33,644 --> 00:09:36,056
So let's try it together, right now.

154
00:09:36,606 --> 00:09:39,162
Sit comfortably and close your eyes.

155
00:09:42,712 --> 00:09:44,367
Breathe in slowly…

156
00:09:48,568 --> 00:09:50,764
and breathe out, long.

157
00:09:56,314 --> 00:09:57,250
Once more.

158
00:09:57,449 --> 00:09:59,105
Breathe in slowly…

159
00:10:03,305 --> 00:10:05,502
and breathe out, long.

160
00:10:11,051 --> 00:10:15,695
Think of one feeling or action lately that you brushed off as just because.

161
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:23,873
Gently find where you feel it in your body.

162
00:10:30,423 --> 00:10:32,979
Ask that feeling, gently.

163
00:10:33,179 --> 00:10:34,043
Why?

164
00:10:42,593 --> 00:10:45,725
If an answer comes, ask that answer too.

165
00:10:45,925 --> 00:10:46,789
Why?

166
00:10:55,339 --> 00:10:57,427
It's okay if no answer comes.

167
00:10:57,627 --> 00:11:00,399
Just by asking, the door has already opened.

168
00:11:04,949 --> 00:11:08,729
Now, to the part of you that holds that reason, say this.

169
00:11:08,929 --> 00:11:09,865
I see.

170
00:11:10,065 --> 00:11:11,145
I understand.

171
00:11:17,695 --> 00:11:19,567
And, I love you.

172
00:11:26,117 --> 00:11:30,113
Feel the warmth spreading through your chest, just as it is.

173
00:11:38,663 --> 00:11:41,075
Now, take a deep breath in…

174
00:11:45,275 --> 00:11:48,911
and as you slowly breathe out, open your eyes.

175
00:11:53,061 --> 00:11:55,293
There is no just because.

176
00:11:55,493 --> 00:11:57,437
You just don't know the reason yet.

177
00:11:57,988 --> 00:12:06,988
The more you come to know those reasons, one by one, the more you understand yourself, the more you love yourself, and the more you create your own life.

178
00:12:07,537 --> 00:12:11,497
And you'll share that overflowing love and abundance with others.

179
00:12:12,047 --> 00:12:15,036
Today, try living just a little more awake.

180
00:12:15,585 --> 00:12:19,906
In the comments, write one just because from today.

181
00:12:20,105 --> 00:12:23,597
And if you found the reason behind it, write that too.

182
00:12:24,147 --> 00:12:25,335
Play your own game.
